    with $\{v,w\}\not\in E(G')$ since $G$ is simple; therefore $\{u,w\}$ cannot belong to a $K_3$ in $G'$, and we have two cases to consider:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item if $\{u, w\}$ belongs to a $K_{1,3}$ in $D'$, that $K_{1,3}$ can be mapped onto a $K_{1,3}$ in $D$ by replacing $\{u,w\}$ with $\{v,w\}$;
        \item otherwise, $\{u,w\}$ is an extremal edge of a $P_4$ in $D'$; since $\{u,w\}\not\in E(G)$, either that edge will remain in a $P_4$ when removing the co-fish and replacing $\{u,w\}$ with $\{v, w\}$, or it will end up in a $K_3$ with either one or two marked edges. Either way, the part can be added as such to $D$.\qed
