I found a second trap beyond the paper’s explicit easy cases: almost every bridgeless cubic graph has a perfect matching, and Proposition 2 then gives an all-\(P_4\) decomposition in polynomial time. The generator therefore needs a certified obstruction to perfect matchings while preserving a planted mixed decomposition. I’m implementing the paper’s co-fish attachment locally around several planted claws; this preserves a known \(\{K_{1,3},P_4\}\)-decomposition and forces selected vertices to be unmatched in any hypothetical perfect matching.
