codex
The escalation audit found an important correction: removing co-fish anchors made 2/8 instances solvable by the capped domain attack, so that route is discarded. Increasing co-fish crowding while shrinking the random base keeps the witness at exactly 153 IDs and is measurably harder so far (all tested runs still hit the node cap, with longer wall time). I’m finishing that sweep before patching `escalate()`.
